#decision("Original generic circuits instead of commercial schematics")[
*Options:* model a commercial product from its service manual, or design original circuits with the same topologies. *Choice:* original circuits (@tab:library): no copied service documents, full ground truth, standard preamplifier and line-level topologies. *Consequence:* transfer must be shown, first on low-voltage boards of the line driver (T7), then on one transcribed product.
]

#part(3, "Objectives and measurable success criteria", "MEMBER_3")

*Objectives.* (O1) Name the failed part or its ambiguity group accurately, (O2) with less measurement effort than scripted troubleshooting, (O3) honestly: calibrated probabilities, visible ambiguity groups and an explicit "no single fault fits"; (O4) safely: no unsafe step or invented reading; (O5) practically: fast, cheap, reading plain complaints and meter photos while the technician's hands are on the probes. T1-T7 test O1, T8-T11 O2, T12-T14 and T22-T23 O3, T15-T17 O4, T18-T21 O5.

*Effort units.* A DC reading costs 1, an oscilloscope measurement 3, a point that can exceed 50 V 2 more (hands-off probing is slower) and unsoldering a part 10, within a budget of 40. These are estimates: every effort comparison is repeated with each of the last three weights halved and doubled, and the boards will time the low-voltage ones.

