#decision("Safety and security rules live in code, not only in the prompt")[
*Options:* instruct the model to be safe, or enforce safety in code. *Choice:* code: prompt injection ranks first in the OWASP Top 10 for LLM applications \[54\] and injected text can steer a model from its instructions \[55\], so notes, complaints and photo text are data and the model's tools act only on the session. *Consequence:* warnings, refusals and locks behave the same in every mode; T15 checks them at every step.
]

